OL,3,GNEWSAStriking doctors warn staff will
OL,4,Aleave NI for better pay
OL,5,
OL,6,FDoctors involved in a 24-hour strike
OL,7,Fover pay have warned more health staff
OL,8,Fwill leave Northern Ireland for higher
OL,9,Fwages and better conditions elsewhere.
OL,11,FSeamus Crumley is among medics who
OL,12,Fjoined a picket line in Belfast after
OL,13,Ftheir union, the British Medical
OL,14,FAssociation (BMA), rejected a pay rise
OL,15,Foffer of 3.5%.
OL,17,FHe moved to Northern Ireland from his
OL,18,Fnative Scotland last year but told BBC
OL,19,FNews NI that despite securing a more
OL,20,Fsenior role he "took a pay cut to come
OL,21,Fhere".
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
